What is Object Storage?

Object storage stores data as objects instead of files in folders or blocks on disk.

Each object contains:

File data
Metadata
Unique object name (key)

Example:

Bucket: employee-documents

Object:
resume.pdf

Metadata:
Size: 2 MB
Uploaded By: Abdullah
Created: Today
Buckets

A bucket is like a top-level container.

Example:

company-files
│
├── images/
├── invoices/
├── videos/
└── documents/

Common buckets:

profile-images
videos
documents
backups
logs
